  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> be a polynomial of degree four and having its extreme values at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></munder><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math> is equal to&nbsp;</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "5iGgA",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>",
